"""A label/list-boundary approximation using punctuation and the current line.

Predict negative activations for colons after short labels, list dashes, and
closing title/bold punctuation. Bold-plus-colon tokens are strongest; numbered
and capitalized labels are stronger than prose or code. Distinguish fused
punctuation and line endings. Some Markdown opening forms get small positive
values; ordinary words and unrecognized forms get zero.

