"""Component layers.0.mlp.down_proj:2576 (negative-going "label punctuation" detector).

What it does: this component goes negative on punctuation that introduces a label,
a heading or a list item, and stays near zero elsewhere. Its activation is largest on:
  * a colon that ends a numbered list heading ("3. Big Data Analytics:"), about -1.2;
  * a colon after a short title-case heading or field name ("Snow Queen:", "Photo:"),
    about -0.85; a colon after a short lower-case phrase or after a long line, about -0.4;
  * a colon after a bracket or parenthesis ("[57]:", "(kbytes):"), about -0.8;
  * a bullet dash ("-", "–") that opens a line, about -0.8.
Colons inside code or quoted strings (lines containing ( ) { } [ ] ; = < > " \\) are
near zero, about -0.15. Mid-line dashes are about -0.1. Everything else is 0.

Why: the program is the explanation. It only reads the current line typed so far, so it
is causal and uses no table of token ids: just punctuation and simple properties of the
line (is it numbered, is it short, does it start with a capital, is it code).

Main program: `step` keeps the current line's text; on each token it looks up the rule above.
"""
import re

READS = ()

LABEL_COLONS = {":", "：", "):", "]:", "）:"}
DASHES = {"-", "–"}
CODE_CHARS = set("(){}[];=<>\"\\")


def step(carry, prefix, upstream):
    if carry is None or prefix.document_ids[-1] != carry["doc"]:
        carry = {"doc": prefix.document_ids[-1], "line": ""}
    tok = prefix.token_strings[-1]
    line = carry["line"]
    stripped = line.strip()
    bare = tok.strip(" ")
    value = 0.0
    if bare in LABEL_COLONS:
        if re.match(r"^\s*\d+[.)]", line):
            value = -1.2  # numbered list heading: "3. Title:"
        elif bare not in (":", "："):
            value = -0.8  # "[57]:", "(kbytes):"
        elif any(ch in CODE_CHARS for ch in line):
            value = -0.15  # colon inside code or a quoted string
        elif len(line.split()) <= 5:
            if stripped[:1].isupper() or stripped[:1] in "-•#|✓":
                value = -0.85  # short title-case heading or label: "Snow Queen:"
            else:
                value = -0.4
        else:
            value = -0.4
    elif bare in DASHES:
        value = -0.8 if stripped == "" else -0.1  # bullet dash starting a line
    if "\n" in tok:
        carry["line"] = ""
    else:
        carry["line"] = line + tok
    return carry, float(value)

