"""Non-sentence dots: decimals, numbered items, spaced dots and dot leaders.

Ordinary sentence stops are nearly silent. Numeric dots are negative, especially
in quoted/bracketed numbers and code. Space-prefixed dots are much stronger, but
a run of spaced dots becomes a positive dot leader. Responses are more negative
near the start of a document. Smaller rules cover doubled dots and dot paths.
