The largest response is to 'always' and its translations. Common adverbs,
universal quantifiers, affirmative answers, and phrases such as 'at least'
also respond. Case and nearby grammatical words adjust a few strong English
triggers. Several material words have a negative response instead.

Only the previous token is retained, resetting at each document. Unlisted
words and finer contextual effects are omitted, rather than memorized.
"""
READS = ()

