"""Adverbs that qualify a verb or clause by how often, how surely, or how
universally something holds: "always", "also", "already", "still", "usually",
"probably", "maybe", "certainly", "such", "just", and the same words in other
languages (sempre, siempre, всегда, immer, いつも, 总是, 也是, 还是, toujours).
Each word class has a fixed strength; the strongest is "always" (about 6.4), then
frequency adverbs (about 1.6), then hedging and modal adverbs (about 0.9), and a
looser group of "typically / generally / actually / everyone"-type words (about
0.6). Every other token, including most -ly manner adverbs ("quickly") and
quantifiers ("only", "all", "not"), outputs 0.
"""

READS = ()

ALWAYS = {
    "always", "sempre", "siempre", "всегда", "immer", "いつも", "总是",
    "toujours", "永远", "常に",
}
FREQUENCY = {
